course: dictionary
lesson: 13936
title: Strict or lenient
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lenient is an adjective. It describes a person who is not strict. A lenient person is gentle when they decide on rules or punishments. The opposite is strict, which means firm and hard to please.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Mrs Patel is lenient, so she lets us finish our drawings after lunch.» The word so tells you that the teacher allows something extra. Ask yourself what would fit: gentle and not firm about rules. That fits.
explain: In law and the news, lenient has a special meaning. «The judge was lenient and gave him a short sentence.» A short sentence is a lighter punishment than people expected, so lenient means giving a lighter punishment than expected.
fact: Lenient means not strict.
fact: A lenient person is gentle when they punish people or make them follow rules.
fact: A lenient sentence is a lighter punishment than expected.
fact: The opposite of lenient is strict.
fact: You will meet phrases like «a lenient teacher», «lenient with» someone, and «a lenient sentence».
exercise: «Mrs Patel is lenient, so she lets us finish our drawings after lunch.» What does lenient mean here? | Always late | Very loud and angry | *Not strict, and gentle about rules | Strict and firm about every rule
exercise: «The judge was lenient and gave him a short sentence.» What is a lenient sentence? | A longer punishment than people expected | *A lighter punishment than people expected | A sentence written in a poem | A punishment that is never given
exercise: Which word is the opposite of lenient? | Kind | *Strict | Gentle | Cheerful
test: «My dad is strict about homework, but my gran is lenient with me.» Which is true about gran? | She gives the longest homework | She is always angry | She never speaks | *She is gentle and does not push me hard
test: Which sentence uses lenient correctly? | I lenient my lunch every day | The sky is lenient today | Lenient is a colour | *The coach was lenient and let us have a short break
exam: «The head teacher was lenient with the boy who was late, because it was his first time.» Why was the teacher lenient? | Because the boy was rude | Because he wanted the boy sent home | Because she was asleep | *Because it was his first time
